    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Advances in group processes publishes theoretical analyses, reviews, and theory based empirical chapters on group phenomena.  The series adopts a broad conception of &quot;group processes.&quot; This includes work on groups ranging from the very small to the very large, and on classic and contemporary topics such as status, power, exchange, justice, influence, decision-making, intergroup relations and social networks.  Previous contributors have included scholars from diverse fields including sociology, psychology, political science, philosophy, computer science, mathematics and organizational behavior</marc:subfield>
